# Commit & push authorship

Every commit must be attributed **only** to the human developer who authored
the change, using that developer's own configured git identity. The GitHub UI
must show a single author — never "and Cursor" / any other AI agent.

## Rules

- The commit **author and committer** must be the real developer's name and
  email (whatever they have set in their local git config, e.g.
  `git config user.name` / `git config user.email`). Do **not** override or
  hard-code a specific person's identity.
- **Never** author or co-author a commit as an AI agent. In particular, do
  **not** add a `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` trailer (or
  any other AI/agent co-author trailer) to the commit message.
- Cursor's git integration may **append that trailer after `git commit`
  returns**, even when the agent did not pass it. Treat that as an automatic
  rewrite of the message: inspect and strip it **before** any push.
- Checking `git log --format='%an <%ae> | %s'` is **not** enough — `%s` is
  only the subject. GitHub's "Co-authored-by" chip comes from the **message
  body**. Always inspect `%B`.

## After every commit (mandatory)

```bash
git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>%n%B'
```

If the body contains `Co-authored-by: Cursor` (any email) or any other
AI/agent trailer, strip it immediately:

```bash
# Last commit only (not yet pushed, or feature branch you are about to force-push):
git log -1 --format='%B' | sed '/^Co-authored-by: Cursor/d' | git commit --amend -F - --no-edit
```

`--amend` is required here: the environment mutated the message after a
successful commit. Then re-check `%B` until the trailer is gone.

## If a stray trailer was already pushed on a feature branch

```bash
FILTER_BRANCH_SQUELCH_WARNING=1 git filter-branch -f \
  --msg-filter 'sed "/^Co-authored-by: Cursor/d"' \
  origin/main..HEAD
git push --force-with-lease
```

Do **not** force-push `main`/`master`.

## Verify before every push

```bash
git log origin/main..HEAD --format='%h %an <%ae>%n%B'
```

Author must be a real developer. Message body must contain **no**
`Co-authored-by: Cursor` (or other AI/agent) line. If any commit still has
it, strip first — do not push.

Each developer sets their own identity once (per developer, not a shared
value):

```bash
git config user.name  "Your Name"
git config user.email "you@tenstorrent.com"
```
